FIX (keeps the authored 1280x720 backdrop intent, SSAO/SSIL enabled everywhere)
Root cause (matches task-2 verdict): MissionPrepUI is built via
MissionPrepUIScript.new() at Control size (0,0) and parented to a CanvasLayer
(ContractTableUI._confirm_prepare). set_anchors_preset(PRESET_FULL_RECT) defaults
to keep_offsets=true, which preserved the zero size down the chain, so the
SubViewportContainer measured (0,0) and crushed the authored 1280x720
SubViewport to the (2,2) engine-minimum floor; with SSIL on that is the exact
godotengine/godot#86631 cascade trigger.

Changed spans (git diff --stat: 2 files, +82/-3):
1) game/src/ui/mission_prep_ui.gd
   - const STAGE_VIEWPORT_SIZE = (1280,720) (was inline Vector2i(1280,720) at :163).
   - _build_all: self + stage_box now set_anchors_preset(PRESET_FULL_RECT, false)
     with zeroed offsets, SIZE_EXPAND_FILL flags, named nodes
     (PrepBackdropContainer / PrepBackdropViewport), and
     stage_box.custom_minimum_size = (1280,720) as a floor (never a shrink
     target; full-rect anchors still stretch to fill larger windows).
   - _ready: resized.connect(_ensure_stage_size) + call_deferred("_ensure_stage_size").
   - new _ensure_stage_size(): re-asserts no-keep-offsets full-rect after layout
     and on resize; if the Control still measures <32px on an axis it takes the
     viewport rect size; any child SubViewport below the authored floor is
     restored to STAGE_VIEWPORT_SIZE. SSIL/SSAO env code untouched
     (ssil_enabled=true site still at mission_prep_ui.gd:457 post-edit).
2) game/src/ui/contract_table_ui.gd _confirm_prepare (the :518 parentage):
   after add_child(prep), re-asserts prep full-rect with keep_offsets=false and
   zeroed offsets (prep._ready runs during add_child while still (0,0)).

Sizing mechanism: kill the keep_offsets preservation of the (0,0) birth size at
both ends of the parentage (prep root in _build_all + _confirm_prepare after
add_child), floor the container at the authored 1280x720 minimum, and re-check
deferred + on resized. The SubViewportContainer then delivers a real non-zero
size to the child SubViewport instead of crushing it to (2,2).

SSAO/SSIL posture (grep, unchanged): ssil_enabled=true at exactly 3 sites --
weather_profile.gd:420 (mission), mission_prep_ui.gd:457 (prep backdrop),
main_menu.gd:150 (menu). Zero ssao_enabled sites under game/src. NOTHING
disabled, globally or per-viewport. level_loader.gd untouched; mission
controller/guard/wardrobe/ledger/thief/hud files untouched.

